# The M5Stack CoreS3: layered over sdkconfig.defaults, as the CYD's and the
# Touch-LCD-2's files are. ESP32-S3 - 16 MB flash, but 8 MB QUAD PSRAM (NOT the
# octal PSRAM of the other three boards), so the base octal mode is overridden
# below. An ILI9342C 320x240 IPS over SPI (register-compatible with the ILI9341
# init, so it rides display_port_spi.c), an FT6336 touch at 0x38 on the internal
# 12/11 I2C bus, an AXP2101 PMIC (0x34) and an AW9523B IO expander (0x58) that
# drive the panel reset and the DLDO1 backlight. The audio amp is an AW88298
# (not ES8311): audio stub. Both IMU drivers are off - the CoreS3 carries a
# BMI270 (and the SE carries none), neither yet supported; the firmware must not
# assume an IMU is present.
#
#   idf.py -B build_cores3 -D SDKCONFIG=build_cores3/sdkconfig \
#          -D SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.defaults.cores3" build
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_BOARD_CORES3=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_SH8601=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_ILI9341=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_TOUCH_FT3168=y
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_AUDIO_ES8311=n
# No supported IMU on this board yet (BMI270 on the CoreS3, none on the SE):
# both drivers off, so the picture-flip / handling detector stay inert and the
# firmware does not wait on an IMU that may be absent.
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_QMI8658=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_MPU6050=n
CONFIG_POCKET_TANK_IMU_AUTO_FLIP=n
# PSRAM: QUAD, overriding the base octal mode (M5Stack CoreS3 is 8 MB quad).
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT=n
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_QUAD=y
